WEBVTT

00:00:04.230 --> 00:00:08.690
Labor: A robot specifically designed
for construction work.

00:00:09.320 --> 00:00:11.990
Labors allow dramatic advances
in construction...

00:00:11.990 --> 00:00:13.700
but also in crime.

00:00:14.030 --> 00:00:15.950
To combat these
new Labor crimes...

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:19.620
the police created a special unit:
The Patrol Labor.

00:00:19.910 --> 00:00:22.540
And thus, the birth of Patlabor.

00:00:48.610 --> 00:00:51.190
yume wo sutenaide
You must not let go of your dreams

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.990
me wo sorasanaide
And never turn your gaze away

00:00:54.990 --> 00:00:58.990
futari no ai mo kumoru yo
Yet even still love may cloud up and fade away

00:01:00.490 --> 00:01:03.370
utsumuita kata wo
And even though you comforted your love

00:01:03.500 --> 00:01:06.370
dakishimeta keredo
When he was feeling down

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:11.210
samishisa mune ni tsumotta
Sadness was still weighing down his heavy heart

00:01:12.670 --> 00:01:18.430
yume wa kimi no buki no hazu da yo
Hang on tight to your dreams - they're weapons in your arsenal

00:01:18.640 --> 00:01:25.020
nee da kara kanashimi mo kinukete itte
You'll find that you can get through anything at all

00:01:25.640 --> 00:01:31.360
so never cry itsu mo kimi wo mitsumete 'ru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be watching over you

00:01:32.190 --> 00:01:37.150
fair na ikikata no kimi ga suki
What I love about you is your strong sense of fairness

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:43.700
so never cry itsu mo kimi no soba ni iru yo
So never cry - you know I will always be right there by your side

00:01:44.500 --> 00:01:49.380
da kara mata asu e kakedashite
And so now you can face your future fearlessly

00:01:57.130 --> 00:02:01.140
Eve's Trap

00:03:59.510 --> 00:04:00.380
Grandma?

00:04:04.340 --> 00:04:04.970
Grandma?

00:04:06.890 --> 00:04:08.100
You'll catch cold.

00:04:08.560 --> 00:04:11.640
I was dreaming
of a time long ago.

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:16.270
I'll be gone for about two hours.
I'm sorry to leave you alone.

00:04:16.980 --> 00:04:18.480
Don't mind me.

00:04:18.980 --> 00:04:20.940
Think about
what you'd like for dinner.

00:04:48.930 --> 00:04:51.020
Entering port at 1700 hours.

00:05:00.360 --> 00:05:02.860
I can't believe it!
Not on our day off!

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:06.490
How can you have
a banquet in the freezing cold?

00:05:06.570 --> 00:05:09.780
Ota, you're the one
who was lonely on Christmas.

00:05:09.870 --> 00:05:11.830
Aren't you glad
we're all here celebrating?

00:05:11.950 --> 00:05:14.870
I'm not one to get taken in
by some weird festival.

00:05:14.870 --> 00:05:16.330
If you don't like it,
then go home.

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:17.830
I'll stay for the grub.

00:05:18.000 --> 00:05:22.250
Shinshi's with his wife, and
Kanuka's with her grandmother.

00:05:22.590 --> 00:05:25.300
It's the only time of year
I actually miss my family.

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:28.390
Hey.

00:05:28.720 --> 00:05:31.180
Don't forget that
you're all still on standby,

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:32.770
even when you're off-duty.

00:05:32.970 --> 00:05:33.600
Yes, sir!

00:05:34.600 --> 00:05:36.140
Kanuka dropped off a present.

00:05:36.350 --> 00:05:38.100
Oh, is she here?

00:05:38.270 --> 00:05:41.770
Yeah, but she left.
She dropped off a half-finished report.

00:05:44.690 --> 00:05:47.910
A real policeman doesn't
chase after women like that!

00:05:49.570 --> 00:05:50.700
Asuma!

00:06:13.970 --> 00:06:15.600
Why'd you tag along?

00:06:15.720 --> 00:06:17.940
Well, what are you
doing here, Asuma?

00:06:18.060 --> 00:06:21.360
Like I said, Kanuka
doesn't know Tokyo too well...

00:06:21.610 --> 00:06:23.940
so I promised to
show her grandmother around.

00:06:24.530 --> 00:06:26.280
- Oh, really?
- Well...

00:06:26.490 --> 00:06:29.700
What are you really up to?
Confess!

00:06:30.700 --> 00:06:33.200
She said she went looking for
the Christmas of 50 years ago.

00:06:34.080 --> 00:06:35.660
The Christmas of 50 years ago?

00:06:35.790 --> 00:06:36.830
What does that mean?

00:06:37.410 --> 00:06:38.370
I don't know.

00:06:38.830 --> 00:06:42.130
Grandma left that message
and then headed out.

00:07:44.020 --> 00:07:45.560
So you finally made it.

00:08:08.340 --> 00:08:11.670
Four Brocken machines and
the experimental one have arrived.

00:08:12.260 --> 00:08:14.840
The experimental one
will be called the "phantom."

00:08:15.300 --> 00:08:18.310
Repeat, the experimental Labor
will be called "phantom."

00:08:19.430 --> 00:08:22.310
It looks like most of her
belongings are still here.

00:08:22.890 --> 00:08:25.850
So, she probably wasn't going far.

00:08:26.860 --> 00:08:29.190
She'll probably be back soon.

00:08:33.490 --> 00:08:34.910
Grandpa's picture is gone.

00:08:35.450 --> 00:08:38.910
What does that mean,
when Grandpa's picture is gone?

00:08:39.450 --> 00:08:41.830
I've a feeling
she's not coming back.

00:08:42.000 --> 00:08:42.960
No way!

00:08:43.080 --> 00:08:46.170
You're just worrying for nothing.
You shouldn't say such things.

00:08:46.250 --> 00:08:50.170
But why did she take Grandpa's picture
if she just went out for a minute?

00:08:50.250 --> 00:08:52.050
Maybe she wanted to
show it to someone.

00:08:52.300 --> 00:08:53.630
I'm not convinced.

00:08:54.800 --> 00:08:56.180
Anyway, let's go look for her.

00:08:56.510 --> 00:08:57.640
How?

00:09:00.310 --> 00:09:03.060
Hello, Special Vehicles,
Second Section. Oh, Shinohara!

00:09:03.270 --> 00:09:04.890
Sorry to disturb.

00:09:05.020 --> 00:09:07.480
But they upgraded
our status to alert standby.

00:09:08.020 --> 00:09:09.940
Return immediately.

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:12.860
- Captain, we, uh...
- What?

00:09:13.110 --> 00:09:15.860
We, uh...

00:09:16.200 --> 00:09:18.370
Uh, never mind.
We're on our way.

00:09:19.580 --> 00:09:21.080
We've received
an alert standby order?

00:09:22.580 --> 00:09:23.250
Let's go.

00:09:23.790 --> 00:09:25.580
But Kanuka,
what about your grandmother?

00:09:26.080 --> 00:09:29.000
I pride myself on
being a professional policewoman.

00:09:43.350 --> 00:09:44.890
Patrol car 504.

00:09:45.520 --> 00:09:48.310
Come in headquarters.
Headquarters?

00:09:49.690 --> 00:09:51.110
I wonder what's wrong?

00:10:31.150 --> 00:10:33.770
Division 2...

00:10:34.270 --> 00:10:37.440
you've just received
an invitation to our party.

00:10:41.660 --> 00:10:45.660
Brocken

00:10:47.660 --> 00:10:50.670
Seadog

00:10:52.210 --> 00:10:53.710
I'm Matsui,
from the Joto Department.

00:10:53.750 --> 00:10:56.590
We received your message.
What's the situation?

00:10:57.010 --> 00:11:01.090
All communications with
Tokyo Teleport have been cut off.

00:11:02.340 --> 00:11:07.560
The phones and networks are down.
Even the radio's out.

00:11:07.890 --> 00:11:11.560
Furthermore, no cars are coming
out of Tokyo Teleport as well.

00:11:11.980 --> 00:11:16.110
As for the connector bridge,
we sent people across...

00:11:16.360 --> 00:11:17.860
but none seem to come back.

00:11:18.690 --> 00:11:20.490
The same goes for vehicles.

00:11:20.570 --> 00:11:23.070
Does that include patrol cars?

00:11:23.240 --> 00:11:23.740
Yes.

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:28.500
Doesn't HQ have
a special anti-hijacking unit?

00:11:28.790 --> 00:11:34.290
The Japanese GSG-9?
I haven't heard from them.

00:11:35.380 --> 00:11:38.800
Well, they don't tend to
keep a high profile, after all.

00:11:39.010 --> 00:11:41.430
But I'd say
they haven't been able to help,

00:11:41.470 --> 00:11:43.220
considering that
you're here to see us.

00:11:43.340 --> 00:11:46.600
What could possibly be
going on at Tokyo Teleport?

00:11:48.930 --> 00:11:51.480
That's what I want
you to find out.

00:11:52.060 --> 00:11:54.020
I'm afraid
it doesn't interest me.

00:11:54.100 --> 00:11:56.270
What are you talking about?
It's our duty.

00:11:57.940 --> 00:12:03.360
And it may be a problem
if we can't get Division 2 involved.

00:12:03.570 --> 00:12:06.950
Clearly, ECM is being used
to jam our communications.

00:12:07.080 --> 00:12:09.700
In other words,
this may be strategic.

00:12:09.830 --> 00:12:11.790
The self-defense force
sounds nervous.

00:12:12.290 --> 00:12:16.080
I wouldn't be surprised
if they mobilized very soon.

00:12:16.920 --> 00:12:18.380
The self-defense force?

00:12:24.840 --> 00:12:27.890
Once the heavy vehicles are armed,
move out!

00:12:27.970 --> 00:12:29.430
Standby at the
Ariake Interchange.

00:12:29.810 --> 00:12:30.720
Get ready!

00:12:31.310 --> 00:12:33.560
Captain Fuwa, phone call!

00:12:41.030 --> 00:12:44.910
Hello? Shinobu!
It's been a while. What's up?

00:12:45.450 --> 00:12:46.320
Nothing, really.

00:12:46.660 --> 00:12:49.580
I was wondering if you had to
work on Christmas Eve.

00:12:50.370 --> 00:12:55.290
We're on duty here, too.
We both have rotten hours.

00:12:56.250 --> 00:12:59.630
Sure, I'd love to see you
at New Year's. Take care.

00:13:01.130 --> 00:13:02.340
She's on the move.

00:13:05.430 --> 00:13:09.300
You never make personal calls
when you're on duty, Shinobu.

00:13:09.810 --> 00:13:14.060
You were checking up on me,
but I won't let you spoil this chance.

00:13:16.310 --> 00:13:18.020
That's bad.

00:13:18.310 --> 00:13:20.520
You have to let Kanuka off tonight,
considering her state.

00:13:20.690 --> 00:13:23.780
We don't have anyone
who can take her place, though.

00:13:24.150 --> 00:13:27.950
Captain, can't we go look for
Kanuka's grandmother?

00:13:29.450 --> 00:13:30.660
What a dilemma.

00:13:42.210 --> 00:13:43.510
I have a favor to ask.

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:49.510
- You want Shige?
- Yeah, just for a while.

00:13:49.640 --> 00:13:52.970
Goto, I don't think
that's a reasonable request.

00:13:53.220 --> 00:13:55.270
I know,
but I'm asking anyway.

00:14:04.530 --> 00:14:06.190
Make sure
you check it thoroughly!

00:14:06.360 --> 00:14:09.240
And ammo!
I need lots of extra ammo!

00:14:09.570 --> 00:14:12.620
I heard this might be an alien
invasion, so don't hold back!

00:14:12.910 --> 00:14:16.290
I had no idea you had
such an imagination, Ota.

00:14:16.620 --> 00:14:17.620
I'm serious!

00:14:18.210 --> 00:14:21.790
The boys are acting strange.
Are you asking me because of that?

00:14:22.290 --> 00:14:23.800
Yes.

00:14:24.170 --> 00:14:27.720
All right. I expect an explanation
when this is over.

00:14:27.880 --> 00:14:28.630
Thanks.

00:14:31.220 --> 00:14:36.060
What does "the Christmas of
50 years ago" mean to you?

00:14:36.560 --> 00:14:40.100
Now you're feeding me riddles?
Who knows?

00:14:41.020 --> 00:14:43.520
Well, thanks anyway.
Who knows?

00:14:44.230 --> 00:14:45.480
Wait.

00:14:46.150 --> 00:14:47.320
50 years ago?

00:14:48.320 --> 00:14:51.160
That would be 1950.

00:14:51.700 --> 00:14:54.620
Isn't that
when the Korean War started?

00:14:55.330 --> 00:14:56.450
The Korean War?

00:14:57.080 --> 00:14:59.000
Beginning that December,

00:14:59.210 --> 00:15:01.210
Japan got a major boost
in its economy...

00:15:01.330 --> 00:15:05.300
as the United States put itself
in an all-out war footing.

00:15:06.000 --> 00:15:08.050
I think it was
around Christmas time.

00:15:33.700 --> 00:15:36.030
You're late, Shinshi.
Oh, Shige!

00:15:36.080 --> 00:15:39.620
Don't worry,
I'm taking Shinshi's place today.

00:15:39.660 --> 00:15:42.620
What's wrong with Shinshi?
That coward!

00:15:42.670 --> 00:15:46.170
No, the Captain assigned him
to something else.

00:15:46.500 --> 00:15:49.050
Well, shall we be going?

00:16:02.770 --> 00:16:04.600
Are you Officer
Mikiyasu Shinshi?

00:16:05.020 --> 00:16:06.730
Yes. Detective Matsui?

00:16:06.860 --> 00:16:08.780
Yes. Nice to meet you.

00:16:10.940 --> 00:16:13.780
Oh, this was the result
of a personal matter.

00:16:13.990 --> 00:16:16.370
So, what are we doing?

00:16:17.030 --> 00:16:18.120
Trying to find a missing person.

00:16:25.540 --> 00:16:28.460
I'll be seeing you
well before New Year's, Shinobu.

00:16:35.640 --> 00:16:36.220
Gomioka!

00:16:39.970 --> 00:16:40.850
Who are you?

00:16:57.660 --> 00:17:01.120
Captain, they should have
sent up the flare by now.

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:02.160
I know.

00:17:03.710 --> 00:17:08.590
They're jamming the radio,
so use loudspeakers for communication.

00:17:08.750 --> 00:17:10.800
Command cars, too.

00:17:11.130 --> 00:17:13.050
Machine 2. Mobilize
and take advance positions.

00:17:13.170 --> 00:17:14.590
Shige, wait here.

00:17:15.050 --> 00:17:18.010
Machine 1 will cross
the bridge. Out.

00:17:20.140 --> 00:17:22.100
If you understand,
then reply!

00:17:22.600 --> 00:17:23.810
- Roger.
- Roger.

00:17:24.810 --> 00:17:25.640
Roger.

00:17:26.520 --> 00:17:27.440
Something's wrong.

00:17:31.230 --> 00:17:32.980
The players are now on stage.

00:17:33.690 --> 00:17:35.360
Places, everyone.

00:17:42.330 --> 00:17:45.370
But it's Christmas vacation!

00:17:45.460 --> 00:17:46.710
Can't you help us somehow?

00:17:47.040 --> 00:17:50.130
Even if you asked around,
it's probably too late.

00:17:50.340 --> 00:17:53.800
How can you say that if you
don't know what we're here for?

00:17:54.300 --> 00:17:55.170
Huh? But...

00:17:55.720 --> 00:17:59.260
Someone's life is at stake!

00:17:59.300 --> 00:18:00.550
But...

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:03.100
Matsui, are you
carrying your revolver?

00:18:04.600 --> 00:18:08.770
This man doesn't understand
that someone's life is in danger!

00:18:09.560 --> 00:18:11.110
Are you threatening me?

00:18:13.190 --> 00:18:15.110
All right! All right, then!

00:18:31.790 --> 00:18:32.590
How horrible!

00:18:41.720 --> 00:18:45.140
It's Machine 1 from Division 1.
Where's Gomioka?!

00:18:50.980 --> 00:18:52.230
He's gone.

00:18:54.770 --> 00:18:56.280
That's Ota! Hurry, Noa!

00:19:16.420 --> 00:19:20.010
Kanuka, why didn't you warn me
that he was behind me!

00:19:20.050 --> 00:19:22.510
Crap! Ota, get away!

00:19:23.510 --> 00:19:26.180
How dare you!
You won't make a fool out of me!

00:19:34.770 --> 00:19:36.440
Why, you!

00:19:57.210 --> 00:20:01.340
A Brocken? What's a West German
military Labor doing here!

00:20:03.760 --> 00:20:04.890
You're under arrest!

00:20:07.060 --> 00:20:10.480
Noa, get back!
You can't take him head-on!

00:20:20.490 --> 00:20:21.990
We're surrounded!

00:20:34.830 --> 00:20:37.210
Ota, there's another one
behind you!

00:20:38.710 --> 00:20:39.420
What?

00:20:45.590 --> 00:20:46.890
What's going on?

00:21:29.390 --> 00:21:30.470
What is this?

00:21:30.640 --> 00:21:35.230
I can't believe it! They're using
an ionizing beam weapon!

00:21:47.450 --> 00:21:49.490
You guys are lucky.

00:21:51.030 --> 00:21:55.000
Rei Clancy,
maiden name Rei Kamimura.

00:21:55.330 --> 00:21:57.080
It sounds like a stage name.

00:21:57.210 --> 00:21:58.920
That doesn't matter.

00:21:59.500 --> 00:22:02.960
Before moving to Hawaii,
she lived in Tachikawa.

00:22:03.210 --> 00:22:04.510
Tachikawa?

00:22:04.800 --> 00:22:08.430
There's a US military base in Tachikawa.
There's a connection there.

00:22:17.770 --> 00:22:21.480
It was Christmas Eve then, too.

00:22:38.290 --> 00:22:39.620
Kanuka!

00:22:42.630 --> 00:22:45.840
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:22:45.960 --> 00:22:49.550
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:22:51.890 --> 00:22:55.810
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:03.230 --> 00:23:05.320
yume ni hikizurare
Pulled into my dream I find that I wake up

00:23:05.440 --> 00:23:08.240
ore wa ase mamire no Lonely
Drenched in sweat and feeling lonely

00:23:08.320 --> 00:23:12.820
hanashi-aite no TV suitchi hipparu
I turn off the TV I've been listening to

00:23:15.490 --> 00:23:17.500
ashita ichinichi wa
Tomorrow I will spend the whole day

00:23:17.580 --> 00:23:20.330
akogareta machi no gomi no naka
In the city of my dreams, amidst the old dust

00:23:20.580 --> 00:23:24.500
hayaku mein sutoriito ni sawaritai no sa
I want to feel the main street beneath my feet soon

00:23:27.670 --> 00:23:31.010
manazashi dake wa itsu demo
I plan to always look on the brighter side

00:23:33.640 --> 00:23:36.260
ue wo muite 'ru tsumori
Keep my chin up, look to the future

00:23:36.220 --> 00:23:38.810
tatta hitotsu no michi da kara
After all, there's only one path I can travel

00:23:38.810 --> 00:23:42.020
dakishimete MIDNIGHT BLUE
Just hold me tightly, Midnight Blue

00:23:42.270 --> 00:23:46.110
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:23:48.480 --> 00:23:52.280
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:23:54.450 --> 00:23:58.330
kon'ya reiji no basu ni nottara
If I can make it to the bus stop by midnight

00:24:00.660 --> 00:24:04.960
ichido-kiri nara dekiru hazu da kara
I know I can do it, if only just once

00:24:06.460 --> 00:24:10.210
This story is fiction...

00:24:06.460 --> 00:24:10.210
but in 10 years, who knows?

00:24:15.010 --> 00:24:19.720
Retreat! Let's get back and tell the
Captain about that identified Labor!

00:24:19.810 --> 00:24:22.980
But, what about Kanuka?!
And Ota's been caught, too!

00:24:23.190 --> 00:24:25.060
What should we do, Asuma?!

00:24:26.400 --> 00:24:29.190
Division 2 is in
a life and death struggle.

00:24:29.610 --> 00:24:33.070
The snow falls on the battleground
at Tokyo Teleport.

00:24:33.570 --> 00:24:37.330
Next time. Eve's Shudder.
Target, locked on!

00:24:36.530 --> 00:24:41.500
Next episode

00:24:36.530 --> 00:24:41.500
Eve's Shudder
